>I have seen alot discussed about co-aligned and non-aligned altars, preistes,
>etc. How do you determine the alignment of a character (not yourself) or an
>object.

	Only altars and creatures even have alignments.  The way to determine
the alignment of an altar or a priest(ess) is with the '/' command.  A co-
aligned altar or priest(ess) is one which is of the same alignment as your
character.  A non-co-aligned altar or preist(ess) is one which is not.  There
are also unaligned altars and priests (two of them) which are unaligned wrt
any character.

>And how do you tell the difference between a throne and an altar, their
>screen symbols are the same.

	If you're playing version 3.0j or later, that should not be the case.
The default is to display thrones as '\' and altars as '_'.

